; Copy these lines into your USER profile npmrc (not this repo).
; Windows:  %USERPROFILE%\.npmrc
; macOS/Linux: ~/.npmrc
;
; 1. Azure DevOps → User settings → Personal access tokens → New Token
;    Scopes: Packaging → Read (or Read & write if you publish)
; 2. Base64-encode the PAT only (PowerShell example below).
; 3. Paste the three lines per registry block (registry + npm paths).

; PowerShell (replace YOUR_PAT):
; [Convert]::ToBase64String([System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes("YOUR_PAT"))

//coderlook.pkgs.visualstudio.com/4ebb65de-f12a-4477-8bb7-6c882034b4a4/_packaging/abdoun-library/npm/registry/:username=VssSessionToken
//coderlook.pkgs.visualstudio.com/4ebb65de-f12a-4477-8bb7-6c882034b4a4/_packaging/abdoun-library/npm/registry/:_password=BASE64_ENCODED_PAT
//coderlook.pkgs.visualstudio.com/4ebb65de-f12a-4477-8bb7-6c882034b4a4/_packaging/abdoun-library/npm/registry/:email=npm requires email to be set but doesn't use the value
//coderlook.pkgs.visualstudio.com/4ebb65de-f12a-4477-8bb7-6c882034b4a4/_packaging/abdoun-library/npm/:username=VssSessionToken
//coderlook.pkgs.visualstudio.com/4ebb65de-f12a-4477-8bb7-6c882034b4a4/_packaging/abdoun-library/npm/:_password=BASE64_ENCODED_PAT
//coderlook.pkgs.visualstudio.com/4ebb65de-f12a-4477-8bb7-6c882034b4a4/_packaging/abdoun-library/npm/:email=npm requires email to be set but doesn't use the value
